# A course as well as a deck: its chapters and steps are subjects of this
# document beside the cards, and every card is a multiple-choice question
# whose back is the correct option and whose distractors are the wrong ones.
<>
    a solid-memo:Deck ,
      dcat:Dataset ,
      schema:Course ;
    dcterms:title "Solid fundamentals"@en ,
                  "Grunderna i Solid"@sv ;
    dcterms:creator <#anton-wiklund> ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dcterms:description "A course on Solid for people who want to build apps with it: why Solid exists, the linked data and RDF it is built on, vocabularies, pods and containers, reading and writing resources, identity and login, access control and sharing, notifications, designing an app's data, building, securing and publishing an app, a minimal app and Solid Memo itself read piece by piece, Solid's open problems, and the Linked Web Storage drafts that may succeed it. 17 chapters of short steps, each a piece of theory, with code and tables where they help, followed by multiple-choice questions; each chapter ends with a review, and every question you answer becomes a card in your deck. The facts come from the Solid specifications, the W3C standards around RDF, the servers' and libraries' documentation and code, and requests recorded on Community Solid Server 7.2, as of October 2026."@en ,
                        "En kurs om Solid för dig som vill bygga appar med det: varför Solid finns, länkade data och RDF som det bygger på, vokabulärer, poddar och behållare, att läsa och skriva resurser, identitet och inloggning, åtkomstkontroll och delning, notiser, hur en app lägger upp sina data, att bygga, säkra och publicera en app, en minimal app och Solid Memo självt lästa bit för bit, Solids öppna problem och Linked Web Storage, som kan efterträda det. 17 kapitel med korta steg av teori följda av flervalsfrågor; varje fråga du besvarar blir ett kort i din kortlek. Kursen finns bara på engelska."@sv ;
