<https://solidproject.org/TR/protocol>
    dcterms:title "Solid Protocol, Version 0.11.0 (Draft Community Group Report)" ;
    dcterms:creator "W3C Solid Community Group" ;
    rdfs:comment "The document's header: \"Copyright © 2019–2024 the Contributors to Solid Protocol, Version 0.11.0, published by the Solid Community Group under the W3C Community Contributor License Agreement (CLA).\" The CLA (https://www.w3.org/community/about/process/cla/), section 2.1, has each contributor grant \"a perpetual (for the duration of the applicable copyright), worldwide, non-exclusive, no-charge, royalty-free, copyright license … to reproduce, prepare derivative works of, publicly display, publicly perform, sublicense, distribute, and implement any Contribution\". Quoted, with the source named in the text, as a short quotation for teaching (Berne Convention article 10(1); in Sweden, 22 § upphovsrättslagen): \"it is not a W3C Standard nor is it on the W3C Standards Track\", \"connects a set of specifications that, together, provide applications with secure and permissioned access to externally stored data in an interoperable way\", \"implicitly has control over all resources in a storage\", \"A URI allocated to a WebID in a Solid storage does not imply that the WebID is the storage owner\", \"to avoid instant propagation of changes all the way to the root container\", \"Paths ending with a slash denote a container resource\", \"There is a 1-1 correspondence between containment triples and relative reference within the path name hierarchy.\", \"it is not possible to create orphan resources\", \"descriptive metadata, authorization conditions, data shape constraints, digital rights or provenance\", \"MUST NOT happen via CORS\", \"Servers MUST conform to either or both\". Otherwise used for facts only. Reliability: normative (CG draft, not W3C standards track). Used for: The backbone of the course: pods, storages, containers, slash semantics, auxiliary resources, Link headers, content negotiation, PUT/POST/PATCH/DELETE rules, N3 Patch, status codes, WAC-or-ACP requirement, WebID-TLS vs Solid-OIDC, and the \"not on the W3C Standards Track\" status. Round 2: §N3 Patch quoted for blank nodes and 422. Round 3: version, date and \"not on the W3C Standards Track\" re-read."@en .

