    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "Your app POSTs a photo to a Solid container with `Slug: holiday` and `Content-Type: image/jpeg`. The `Location` is `/photos/holiday`, with no extension. How should a gallery app later tell that it is a JPEG?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "From the `Content-Type` of a HEAD or GET on it"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "A HEAD or GET returns the type the file was stored under in `Content-Type`. URLs need not carry an extension and servers name files differently (NSS 6.0.0 turns `Slug: note` with `text/turtle` into `note.ttl`), so never infer the type from them. As of October 2026 the JavaScript Solid Server (JSS) even serves an extensionless Turtle document received by PUT as `application/octet-stream`, so a surprising type may be the server's doing."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-read-write-6a-d1> ,
