    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Apps can never be restricted; only users can be"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "ACP client matchers restrict apps by client ID where ACP is used."@en .

<#q-sharing-r03>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "After Solid-OIDC login, the pod knows Alice's WebID, the app's client ID and the issuer. Which of these can a plain WAC rule check, and which can an ACP matcher check?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "WAC checks only the WebID; ACP can check all three"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "The access token carries the WebID, the client ID (`client_id`; the ID token calls it `azp`) and the issuer. Plain WAC rules name agents only, while ACP matchers can test `acp:agent`, `acp:client` and `acp:issuer`."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-sharing-r03-d1> ,
                          <#q-sharing-r03-d2> ,
                          <#q-sharing-r03-d3> .

<#q-sharing-r03-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "WAC and ACP can both check all three"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "WAC subjects name agents, groups and classes; it has no client or issuer subject."@en .

<#q-sharing-r03-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "WAC checks the WebID and client ID; only ACP checks the issuer"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "WAC has no client matcher; `acl:origin` uses the browser's Origin header, not the client ID."@en .

<#q-sharing-r03-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Both check only the WebID; the client ID is for login only"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "ACP's `acp:client` and `acp:issuer` matchers test the client ID and issuer."@en .

<#q-sharing-r04>
