<#q-interop-7b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "Your Solid app's TypeScript types are generated from its ShEx shapes with LDO. What does that give you?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Code that is typed against the published data contract."@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Generating types from the shapes keeps the code and the published contract in step, but it can't control what other apps put in the pod."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-interop-7b-d1> ,
                          <#q-interop-7b-d2> ,
                          <#q-interop-7b-d3> .

<#q-interop-7b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "A guarantee that any data read from the pod is valid at run time."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Other apps may have written anything; you still validate at run time."@en .

<#q-interop-7b-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Shape validation on the server for every write."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Code generation runs in your build, not on the pod."@en .

<#q-interop-7b-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Automatic migration of data in older formats."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Migrations are code you write separately."@en .

<#ch-interop-8>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-interop> ;
    schema:position 7 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## SAI and Shape Trees: the next model

Solid Application Interoperability (SAI), a draft Community Group report (as of October 2026), rethinks discovery and access together. Three ideas carry it:

- **An Authorization Agent.** The user's profile names an app that manages access for them (`interop:hasAuthorizationAgent`).
- **Data organised by shape tree.** Data lives in registrations, each a container whose contents conform to one **shape tree**: a template for a tree of resources and the ShEx or SHACL shapes they must match.
- **Need → decision → grant.** An app declares what it needs by shape tree and access mode; the user decides in their agent, which grants the app exactly that data.

| | Type index | SAI |
|---|---|---|
| Unit of agreement | RDF class | Shape tree |
| Who writes it | Each app | The Authorization Agent |
| Access | Separate (WAC/ACP) | Built in: need → decision → grant |

SAI addresses Chapter 9's apps-versus-users problem (Step 9.11), but adoption is narrow: ActivityPods, a Solid-based ActivityPub server, implements its application registrations, and a 2024 community summary found type indexes "the only one you can use in practice"."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-interop-8a> ,
                         <#q-interop-8b> .

<#q-interop-8a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
