<#q-building-apps-8b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "On a shared computer, a user clicks \"Log out\" in a Solid app, which calls `logout({ logoutType: \"app\" })`. The next person clicks \"Log in\" and is in her account without typing a password. Why?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Her provider session is still alive"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "App logout forgets the session in your app only; offer provider logout (`logoutType: \"idp\"`) to end it at the provider too. ⚠ On CSS 7.2 (2026) the password returned only after she also logged out on its account page."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-building-apps-8b-d1> ,
                          <#q-building-apps-8b-d2> ,
                          <#q-building-apps-8b-d3> .

<#q-building-apps-8b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "The library kept her tokens in localStorage"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The library keeps tokens in memory only, and app logout cleared them."@en .

<#q-building-apps-8b-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "The pod remembered her from her last request"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Pods check each request's token; they hold no login session."@en .

<#q-building-apps-8b-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Her DPoP key was still cached with the page"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "A key alone is no login; the provider issued fresh tokens."@en .

<#ch-building-apps-9>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-building-apps> ;
    schema:position 8 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Hosting a Client ID Document

A Client ID Document describes your app to identity providers. Hosting one has four rules:

1. **Its URL is the `client_id`** you pass to `login()`. Serve it over HTTPS, with `client_id` inside set to exactly that URL.
2. **Serve JSON-LD:** `Content-Type: application/ld+json`, with the context `https://www.w3.org/ns/solid/oidc-context.jsonld`.
3. **List redirect URIs exactly.** Providers compare a `redirect_uri` with `redirect_uris` as exact strings, so `/callback` and `/callback/` differ. Add `post_logout_redirect_uris` for provider logout.
4. **Keep it reachable.** Providers fetch it at login, so while it is down nobody can log in.

⚠ CSS 7.2 keeps no copy and can fetch it again at every lookup, which normally includes silent restores and token refreshes, so there an outage can also end each session at its next refresh (within the access token's 3600 s). Other providers may cache it.

On CSS 7.2, a login with a `redirect_uri` the document didn't list was refused before any token existed:

```text
400 {"name":"InvalidRedirectUri","message":"invalid_redirect_uri", …}
```

**Local development.** The spec requires HTTPS, and a hosted provider cannot reach your `localhost`. So develop with `clientName` (dynamic registration), and switch to the Client ID Document when you deploy.

⚠ CSS 7.2 also accepts an `http://localhost` client ID such as `http://localhost:5173/id.jsonld`, but answers an `http://127.0.0.1` client ID with a 500 error ("SSL is required for client_id authentication unless working locally.")."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-building-apps-9a> ,
                         <#q-building-apps-9b> .

<#q-building-apps-9a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
