<#ch-building-apps-10>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-building-apps> ;
    schema:position 9 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Reading and writing with @inrupt/solid-client

`@inrupt/solid-client` (v4) models an RDF document as a **SolidDataset** and one subject inside it as a **Thing**. Both are **immutable**: every setter returns a *new* object, and nothing reaches the pod until you save.

```js
import { getSolidDataset, getThing, setStringNoLocale, setThing,
  saveSolidDatasetAt } from "@inrupt/solid-client";

const NAME = "http://schema.org/name";      // a predicate is just an IRI
let ds = await getSolidDataset(url, { fetch: session.fetch });   // read
let card = getThing(ds, `${url}#card1`);  // null if the Thing isn't in the document
card = setStringNoLocale(card, NAME, "Bonjour");                  // new Thing
ds = setThing(ds, card);                                          // new dataset
await saveSolidDatasetAt(url, ds, { fetch: session.fetch });      // write
```

Change the Thing, put it back with `setThing`, then save. Skip `setThing` and the change is silently lost. If the document has no `#card1`, the setter throws `Expected a Thing, but received: [null].`, so check for `null` first and create a missing Thing with `createThing`.

Notice `{ fetch: session.fetch }` on every call that talks to the pod. The browser's built-in `fetch` is not authenticated. Leave the option out, or pass the global `fetch` by mistake, and the library sends anonymous requests that see only public data: a classic beginner bug.

For sharing, use the library's universal access API, and check what `universalAccess.setAgentAccess` returns: on CSS 7.2 with ACP, for a resource with no ACR yet, it returned `null` and shared nothing."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-building-apps-10a> ,
                         <#q-building-apps-10b> .

<#q-building-apps-10a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front """This `@inrupt/solid-client` (v4) code runs without error, but the pod never changes. What is missing?

```js
let ds = await getSolidDataset(url, { fetch: session.fetch });
let card = getThing(ds, `${url}#card1`);
card = setStringNoLocale(card, "http://schema.org/name", "Bonjour");
await saveSolidDatasetAt(url, ds, { fetch: session.fetch });
```"""@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Putting the changed Thing back with `setThing`"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Setters return new immutable objects, so the dataset saved here still holds the original Thing. `ds = setThing(ds, card)` fixes it."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-building-apps-10a-d1> ,
                          <#q-building-apps-10a-d2> ,
                          <#q-building-apps-10a-d3> .

<#q-building-apps-10a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "A call that commits the Thing to the pod directly"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Things are saved only as part of a dataset; the dataset still holds the old Thing."@en .

<#q-building-apps-10a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "A `fetch` option on the `setStringNoLocale` call"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Setters work locally and need no fetch; only reads and saves talk to the pod."@en .

<#q-building-apps-10a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Reloading the dataset before saving it again"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Reloading would only fetch the unchanged data; the edit must be placed into the dataset."@en .

<#q-building-apps-10b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "A logged-in user's private document returns 401 when your Solid app calls `getSolidDataset(url)` from `@inrupt/solid-client` (v4). What is the most likely cause?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "The session's `fetch` was not passed to the call"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Without `{ fetch: session.fetch }` the request is anonymous, so private resources answer 401."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-building-apps-10b-d1> ,
                          <#q-building-apps-10b-d2> ,
                          <#q-building-apps-10b-d3> .

<#q-building-apps-10b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "`getSolidDataset` can only read public documents"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "It reads private documents when given an authenticated fetch."@en .

<#q-building-apps-10b-d2>
