<#ch-security-7>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-security> ;
    schema:position 6 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Acting for a user over time: offline_access and refresh tokens

A backend sometimes must act **as a particular user** while she is away; otherwise give it its own WebID (Step 13.6). Add the `offline_access` scope to the code flow. A provider that supports it returns a **refresh token**, which the backend exchanges for new access tokens later.

⚠ On CSS 7.2 (October 2026), refresh tokens last a day and come only if the user leaves "Remember this client" ticked.

⚠ As of October 2026, Inrupt's Node library (v5.0.1) requests `offline_access` by default.

**The backend runs the login itself**, keeping the tokens and DPoP key on the server. On CSS 7.2 (October 2026), with a local origin for `notes.example`, this code got a refresh token:

```js
import { Session, EVENTS, refreshTokens } from "@inrupt/solid-client-authn-node";
// GET /login (Express-style): one Session per user, its id kept in a cookie
const session = new Session({ keepAlive: false });
await session.login({
  oidcIssuer, clientId: "https://notes.example/id.jsonld",  // your Client ID Document
  redirectUrl: "https://notes.example/auth/callback",
  handleRedirect: (url) => res.redirect(url),                 // send her to her provider
});
// GET /auth/callback: get her Session back from a Map keyed by the cookie's id,
// keep her tokens with session.events.on(EVENTS.NEW_TOKENS, (tokens) => store(tokens)), then
await session.handleIncomingRedirect(`https://notes.example${req.url}`);
```

Later, `refreshTokens(stored)` returns new tokens, and `buildAuthenticatedFetch(accessToken, { dpopKey })` from `@inrupt/solid-client-authn-core` reads her pod with them.

Treat a refresh token like a password:

- Keep it **server-side**, encrypted, with its DPoP key.
- Expect **rotation**: a refresh may return a new token and invalidate the old one; store the newest.
- On `invalid_grant`, delete the token and ask her to log in again.

⚠ On CSS 7.2 (October 2026), a DPoP-bound refresh token rotates only after 70% of its lifetime; elsewhere, possibly on every refresh."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-security-7a> ,
                         <#q-security-7b> .

<#q-security-7a>
