<#ch-security-8>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-security> ;
    schema:position 7 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Receiving webhooks safely

With **WebhookChannel2023** your backend subscribes with an `https` `sendTo` URL, and the server POSTs notifications there. The response's `sender` names the WebID the server will authenticate as, and the draft requires an authenticated request "using identity provided as *sender*". How a receiver checks that is left open in the Notifications specification's issue tracker (issue #155).

⚠ On CSS 7.2 (October 2026), the server sends `Authorization: DPoP <token>` with a DPoP proof; the token's `webid` is a WebID the server serves for itself, naming the server as issuer. Verify it as a pod does, with a library such as `@solid/access-token-verifier`, and test against each server. On CSS this token's `iss` has no trailing slash (`http://localhost:3000`), unlike its login issuer, so an exact string comparison rejects genuine webhooks.

So don't rely on sender checks alone:

- Use an **unguessable URL per subscription**, such as `https://hooks.example/solid/3f9c…`, and reject POSTs to unknown ones.
- Treat the body as a **hint**. Refetch the topic with your own credentials; a DPoP proof doesn't cover the body anyway.
- **Answer quickly** with a 2xx and do the work afterwards.
- **Unsubscribe** when done; on CSS, DELETE the channel's `id`."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-security-8a> ,
                         <#q-security-8b> .

<#q-security-8a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "A Solid WebhookChannel2023 POST tells your backend that a resource it watches was updated. What should the backend do next?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Refetch the resource with its own credentials"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "A notification says something changed. What changed, and whether it really did, comes from reading the resource yourself."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-security-8a-d1> ,
                          <#q-security-8a-d2> ,
                          <#q-security-8a-d3> .

<#q-security-8a-d1>
