    solid-memo:distractorNote "That token identifies the pod server, not your backend."@en .

<#q-security-8b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "How a Solid WebhookChannel2023 receiver checks the sender isn't standardised, and servers differ. Which defence works whatever server sends the POST?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "An unguessable URL per subscription, plus refetching the topic"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "A secret URL keeps strangers from reaching your handler, and refetching means a forged POST can at most make you read the resource again. Verify the sender's token too where the server supports it."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-security-8b-d1> ,
                          <#q-security-8b-d2> ,
                          <#q-security-8b-d3> .

<#q-security-8b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Checking for an `Authorization` header, then trusting the body"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Anyone can add a header; only a verified token means something, and the body is a hint anyway."@en .

<#q-security-8b-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Accepting POSTs only from the pod server's IP address"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Servers may send from other or shared addresses, and an address says nothing about the body."@en .

<#q-security-8b-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Requiring a signature made with a secret you and the server share"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "WebhookChannel2023 defines no shared secret, so servers don't send one."@en .

<#ch-security-9>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-security> ;
    schema:position 8 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Deploying and publishing your app

A browser-only Solid app is static files, so any static host that serves HTTPS will do; Solid-OIDC requires tokens and credentials to travel only over TLS. Before going live:

- **Client ID Document.** Host it at a stable `https` URL, usually on your app's origin. Its `client_id` must equal that URL, and `redirect_uris` must list your production redirect URLs, which providers match exactly. With a development server on `localhost`, keep using `clientName` instead.
- **Keep it reachable.** Providers fetch it when a user logs in, and may cache it for a while; if it moves or goes down, logins fail.
- **Redirect back to one fixed page**, listed in `redirect_uris`, where `handleIncomingRedirect()` runs; route onward from there, saving the route first. Providers reject unlisted URLs.
- **Send your CSP header** (Step 13.2).
- **Test with accounts from several providers.**

Once live, you can ask for a listing in the app catalogue on solidproject.org.

⚠ As of October 2026, the catalogue takes requests by email, and its criteria include WebID login at a provider of the user's choice and keeping the app's data in pods."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-security-9a> ,
                         <#q-security-9b> .

<#q-security-9a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "After deploying a Solid app to `https://notes.example/`, logins fail with a redirect URI error, though they worked on `localhost`. What is the likely cause?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "The Client ID Document doesn't list the production redirect URL"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Providers compare the redirect URL exactly with the `redirect_uris` in the Client ID Document, so production URLs must be listed."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-security-9a-d1> ,
                          <#q-security-9a-d2> ,
                          <#q-security-9a-d3> .

<#q-security-9a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "The pod refuses requests from origins it hasn't seen before"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Pods allow every origin through CORS; this error comes from the provider."@en .

<#q-security-9a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Static hosts can't serve the redirect page of a login"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The redirect page is an ordinary page of your app."@en .

<#q-security-9a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Providers accept logins only from apps in the catalogue"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The catalogue is a directory, not a requirement for logging in."@en .

<#q-security-9b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "A deployed Solid app's Client ID Document is at `https://notes.example/id.jsonld`. What must hold for users to keep logging in?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "It stays reachable and lists the redirect URL in use"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Providers fetch the `client_id` URL when a user logs in, possibly from a cache, and check the redirect URL against it, so the document must stay reachable and up to date."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-security-9b-d1> ,
                          <#q-security-9b-d2> ,
                          <#q-security-9b-d3> .

<#q-security-9b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Each user's pod holds a copy and checks the redirect URL"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The provider fetches the `client_id` URL itself and checks the redirect; the pod isn't involved."@en .

<#q-security-9b-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It carries the app's signature for providers to check"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "No signature is defined; the provider trusts the document because it fetched it from the `client_id` URL over https."@en .

<#q-security-9b-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It is served from the same origin as the users' pods"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Apps and pods can be on any hosts; pods allow every origin through CORS."@en .

<#q-security-r01>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "Your Solid backend's webhook handler learns that a post changed, refetches it and finds an `as:image` IRI to make a thumbnail from. What is safe?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Fetch the image only after checking its scheme and resolved address"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Data in a pod is untrusted input, and a backend that fetches URLs from it needs SSRF checks."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-security-r01-d1> ,
                          <#q-security-r01-d2> ,
                          <#q-security-r01-d3> .

<#q-security-r01-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Fetch the image at once, since the post came from your user's pod"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Any agent with write access may have written it, and the IRI may point inside your network."@en .

<#q-security-r01-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Fetch the image only if the webhook POST carried a valid token"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That token says who sent the notification, not where the IRI points."@en .

<#q-security-r01-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Fetch the image only if its IRI parsed as valid RDF"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "An internal address is a perfectly valid IRI."@en .

<#q-security-r02>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "An attacker's literal in a Solid pod, `<img src=x onerror=\"…\">`, ran as script in your web app. Which measure would have prevented it?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Rendering literals with `textContent`"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Escaping output stops the injection; DPoP and memory-only tokens don't, and CSP is a second line of defence."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-security-r02-d1> ,
                          <#q-security-r02-d2> ,
                          <#q-security-r02-d3> .

<#q-security-r02-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Using DPoP-bound access tokens"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "DPoP doesn't stop script running in your page."@en .

<#q-security-r02-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Keeping tokens only in memory"@en ;
