    solid-memo:distractorText "Allowing only `http:` and `https:` link schemes"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That stops `javascript:` links, not markup inside a literal."@en .

<#q-security-r03>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "Three Solid jobs: (1) a nightly backup of your own pod; (2) a public service many people use; (3) syncing one user's pod, acting as her, while she is away. Which pairing fits?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "(1) client credentials as you; (2) its own WebID; (3) a refresh token"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Act as yourself with client credentials, as another user with her refresh token, and as a service with its own WebID. Prefer the service's own WebID whenever the user can grant it narrow access, since its actions stay separate and revocable."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-security-r03-d1> ,
                          <#q-security-r03-d2> ,
                          <#q-security-r03-d3> .

<#q-security-r03-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "(1) a refresh token; (2) client credentials as you; (3) its own WebID"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "A public service acting as you would use your access for everyone."@en .

<#q-security-r03-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "(1) its own WebID; (2) a refresh token; (3) client credentials as you"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Client credentials act as you, not as the user being synced."@en .

<#q-security-r03-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "(1) client credentials as you; (2) a refresh token; (3) its own WebID"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "A service holding everyone's refresh tokens acts as each of them."@en .

<#q-security-r04>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "A look-alike Solid-OIDC issuer copies a real provider's login page. Which protects the pod, and which protects the user?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Pod: the profile must list the issuer; user: seeing the issuer's host"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "The `solid:oidcIssuer` check stops a fake issuer from logging in as other WebIDs; only the user, helped by your app showing the host, can avoid typing her password into it."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-security-r04-d1> ,
                          <#q-security-r04-d2> ,
                          <#q-security-r04-d3> .

