<#ch-read-an-app-7>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 6 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Editing with N3 Patch and `If-Match`

Editing a note means replacing one triple: delete the old `schema:text`, insert the new one (Steps 6.7-6.8). To avoid lost updates the app sends the ETag it read in `If-Match` (Step 6.11). If someone changed the note in between, CSS answers **412**; the app reads the note again, applies the user's change to the *fresh* text, and retries once.

```js
// src/notes.js
export async function editNote(url, change, fetch) {
  let retriedAfter;
  for (let attempt = 1; ; attempt += 1) {
    const { quads, etag } = await readTurtle(url, fetch);
    const it = `${url}#it`;
    const [old] = objects(quads, it, `${ns.schema}text`);
    const body = n3Patch({
      deletes: `<${it}> schema:text ${literal(old)}.`,
      inserts: `<${it}> schema:text ${literal(change(old))}.`,
    });
    // node-solid-server 6 sends no ETag on GET: then only the deletes guard the edit.
    const headers = etag ? { 'if-match': etag } : {};
    try {
      const res = await patch(url, body, fetch, headers);
      return { status: res.status, attempt, retriedAfter, conditional: Boolean(etag) };
    } catch (e) {
      // 412: stale ETag. 409: the text we delete is no longer there. Both mean "changed".
      if (![409, 412].includes(e.status) || attempt === 2) throw e;
      retriedAfter = e.status;
    }
  }
}
```

`change` is a function, not a value, so the retry can decide what to do with whatever text is there now. A change that returns the typed text no matter what would overwrite the other edit: the very lost update `If-Match` caught. So the Edit button asks when the fresh text isn't what the user saw:

```js
// src/main.js (Edit)
await editNote(note.url, (fresh) => (fresh === note.text
  || window.confirm(`Someone changed this note to:\\n\\n${fresh}\\n\\nReplace it with your text?`)
  ? text : fresh), fetch);
```

On CSS 7.2, with another edit made between the read and the PATCH:

```text
plain edit: {"status":205,"attempt":1,"conditional":true}
edit that lost a race, then retried: {"status":205,"attempt":2,"retriedAfter":412,"conditional":true}
text now: Edited elsewhere (and by me)
```

CSS answers a successful PATCH with 205; both edits survive."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-7a> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-7b> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-7c> .

<#q-read-an-app-7a>
