<#ch-read-an-app-8>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 7 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Uploading a picture

A picture is a non-RDF resource (Step 6.6): POST the bytes with their own `Content-Type` (in the browser, the file input's `file.type`) and read `Location`. Its metadata can't go inside a PNG, so the app writes it to the picture's description resource, using an N3 Patch.

The app doesn't build that resource's URL by appending `.meta`: the name is the server's choice (`pixel.meta` on CSS 7.2, `pixel.png.meta` on node-solid-server 6), so it HEADs the picture and follows `rel="describedby"`. It compares relation names without regard to case, because NSS 6 sends `describedBy`. And it only PATCHes: CSS 7.2 allows no PUT on a description resource, whose `Allow` header lists only `OPTIONS, HEAD, GET, PATCH`.

```js
// src/notes.js
export async function uploadPicture(container, bytes, description, fetch, { slug = 'picture', type = 'image/png' } = {}) {
  const res = ok('POST', container, await fetch(container, {
    method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': type, slug }, body: bytes,
  }));
  const url = new URL(res.headers.get('location'), container).href;
  const [describedBy] = linksOf(await fetch(url, { method: 'HEAD' }), 'describedby', url);
  if (describedBy) {
    await patch(describedBy, n3Patch({ inserts: `<${url}> schema:description ${literal(description)}.` }), fetch);
  }
  return { url, describedBy };
}
```

On CSS 7.2 a one-pixel PNG posted with `Slug: pixel` became `…/notes/pixel`, described by `…/notes/pixel.meta`, which then read (`<pixel>` is relative to `…/notes/pixel.meta`):

```turtle
@prefix dc: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>.
@prefix ldp: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#>.
@prefix posix: <http://www.w3.org/ns/posix/stat#>.
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.

<pixel> <http://www.w3.org/ns/ma-ont#format> "image/png";
    a ldp:Resource;
    dc:modified "2026-10-07T21:49:02.189Z"^^xsd:dateTime;
    posix:size "70";
    <http://schema.org/description> "A one-pixel test image".
```

NSS 6 stored `pixel.png` and answered GET on its `.meta` with 404, although the PATCH was stored. To list pictures, an app HEADs each contained resource, keeps those whose `Content-Type` starts with `image/`, and reads `schema:description` from the `describedby` target."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-8a> .

<#q-read-an-app-8a>
