<#ch-read-an-app-9>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 8 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Sharing a note (WAC)

To share a note, `shareNote` follows Step 9.3: check `WAC-Allow` for Control, follow `rel="acl"`, then add a rule to the existing ACL with an insert-only N3 Patch, or create one. A new ACL replaces inheritance (Step 8.6), so it **restates alice's own Read, Write and Control**. An ACP server gets another branch (Step 14.12).

```js
// src/share.js (WAC branch)
  const reader = `<#reader-${crypto.randomUUID()}> a acl:Authorization;
  acl:agent <${friend}>; acl:accessTo <${url}>; acl:mode acl:Read.`;
  if (existing.ok) {
    await patch(rules, n3Patch({ inserts: reader }), fetch); // add to the ACL it already has
  } else {
    // A resource's own ACL replaces the inherited rules (Step 8.6), so restate the owner.
    await put(rules, `@prefix acl: <${ns.acl}>.
<#owner> a acl:Authorization;
  acl:agent <${owner}>; acl:accessTo <${url}>; acl:mode acl:Read, acl:Write, acl:Control.
${reader}`, fetch);
  }
```

On CSS 7.2, bob's GET then got 200 with `WAC-Allow: user="read"`, and his PATCH 403.

⚠ An ACL with only a public-Read rule left alice `WAC-Allow: user="read",public="read"`: PUT on the note, and GET, PUT and DELETE on its ACL, all got 403. CSS 7.2's owner rescue applies only to configurations with storages at the pods, not the default. WAC promises no rescue.

To unshare, the app deletes the friend's authorization triples with one N3 Patch, copied from the ACL it just read: deletes must match exactly. A list several people add to (Step 9.10) needs only Append: each add is an insert-only patch with a fresh `<#item-…>` IRI. On CSS 7.2 bob, with Append and Read, got 205 for an add, 403 for PUT and for deletes, and 422 for a blank node. Two simultaneous adds, by bob and carol, were both kept."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-9a> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-9b> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-9c> .

<#q-read-an-app-9a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
