    solid-memo:front "In WAC, a Solid app creates the first ACL for alice's note to share it with bob. Why does that ACL also contain a rule giving alice Read, Write and Control?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "The note's own ACL replaces inherited rules; she'd lose access"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Once a document has its own ACL, inherited `acl:default` rules no longer apply to it; on CSS 7.2's default configuration, leaving her out cost alice Write on the note and all access to its ACL."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-read-an-app-9a-d1> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-9a-d2> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-9a-d3> .

