<#q-read-an-app-10a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Messages in an inbox are readable by apps only, not users"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Rules name agents; bob reads his messages with his own login."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-10b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "A Solid app archives an inbox message by PUTting a copy into an archive container with `If-None-Match: *`, then DELETEing the original. On a retry, a 412 on the PUT with the same bytes already there means it goes on to the DELETE. The PUT succeeds, but the DELETE fails with a network error. What does the user have?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "The message twice, in the inbox and in the archive"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Copying first means a failure in between leaves a duplicate, never a loss; the retry's 412 shows the copy is already there, so it finishes the DELETE."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-read-an-app-10b-d1> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-10b-d2> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-10b-d3> .

<#q-read-an-app-10b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "No copy at all, because the PUT is rolled back"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Each HTTP request stands alone; nothing undoes the PUT."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-10b-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Only the archived copy, because CSS finishes the delete later"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The DELETE was never confirmed; on CSS 7.2 the inbox still listed the message."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-10b-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "A stuck message: the next attempt gets 412 and stops"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The 412 means the copy is there; the app checks its bytes and goes on to the DELETE."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-10c>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
