    solid-memo:distractorNote "Anyone with Append can put alice's WebID in `actor`."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-10c-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Alice gave bob access to the document, and he may read it"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Her profile is public; bob could read it before any message."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-10c-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Bob's app may show it as \"alice shared this with you\""@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The check can't tell a share from a page that was readable anyway."@en .

<#ch-read-an-app-11>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 10 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Subscribing to changes

To keep the screen current, the app subscribes with **WebSocketChannel2023** (Steps 10.2-10.5 and 10.7). It follows the topic's `storageDescription` link, finds the subscription service whose `notify:channelType` is WebSocketChannel2023, POSTs a subscription, and opens a WebSocket to `receiveFrom`. A message says *that* something changed, not what: on `Update` the app refetches (the message's `state` is the new ETag), on `Delete` it drops the note. If the server offers no such service, `subscribe` returns `null` and the app says "reload to see changes". If the socket closes later, for example because the server restarted, `onClose` lets the app say live updates are off; Step 10.9 covers reconnecting.

```js
// src/live.js
  const { receiveFrom } = await res.json();
  const socket = new WebSocket(receiveFrom);
  socket.onmessage = (event) => {
    const message = JSON.parse(event.data);
    if (/Delete$/.test(message.type)) onDelete(message);
    else onUpdate(message); // Update (state = the new ETag); a container also sends Add, Remove
  };
  await new Promise((resolve, reject) => { socket.onopen = resolve; socket.onerror = reject; });
  socket.onclose = () => onClose();
```

On CSS 7.2, a subscription to one note, which was then edited and deleted, received:

```text
{…,"type":"Update","object":"http://localhost:3000/alice40742/notes/first","state":"\\"1791409742758-text/turtle\\"","published":"2026-10-07T21:49:02.761Z"}
{…,"type":"Delete","object":"http://localhost:3000/alice40742/notes/first","published":"2026-10-07T21:49:02.782Z"}
```

The `state` equalled the ETag a HEAD returned after the edit; the Delete message has no `state`."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-11a> .

<#q-read-an-app-11a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "A Solid app subscribed with WebSocketChannel2023 receives an `Update` message for a note. How does it learn the note's new text?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "It GETs the note again; the message carries no content"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Notifications say that a resource changed (`state` is its new ETag); to see what changed, the app refetches it."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-read-an-app-11a-d1> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-11a-d2> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-11a-d3> .

<#q-read-an-app-11a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It reads the new text from the message's `object` field"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "object is the note's URL, not its content."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-11a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It applies the N3 Patch that comes inside the message"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Messages carry no patch; they only announce the change."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-11a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It waits for a second message listing the changed triples"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "There is no second message; the client must refetch."@en .

<#ch-read-an-app-12>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 11 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Sharing on an ACP server

The same code was run against a second CSS 7.2, configured with Access Control Policy (Step 9.4) instead of WAC.

There `rel="acl"` points to `first.acr`, and a HEAD on it, even a 404, carries `Link: <…acp#AccessControlResource>; rel="type"`. That type, not the URL's suffix, tells `shareNote` to take its ACP branch. ACP only adds (Step 9.4): the pod root's `acp:memberAccessControl` keeps applying, so alice needs no restating. One insert-only N3 Patch creates the ACR (201) or adds to it (205), with fragment IRIs for the access control, policy and matcher, because blank nodes are refused in inserts.

The library route did worse. Step 9.5 introduced `universalAccess.setAgentAccess` as one call for both WAC and ACP. On CSS 7.2 with WAC it worked. With ACP, a new resource has no ACR yet, and the call returned `null` without sharing: bob stayed at 403. Always check its return value.

```js
// src/share.js (ACP branch)
  const id = `${acr}#friend-${crypto.randomUUID()}`;
  await patch(acr, n3Patch({
    inserts: `<${acr}> a acp:AccessControlResource; acp:resource <${url}>; acp:accessControl <${id}>.
<${id}> a acp:AccessControl; acp:apply <${id}-policy>.
<${id}-policy> a acp:Policy; acp:allow acl:Read; acp:anyOf <${id}-matcher>.
<${id}-matcher> a acp:Matcher; acp:agent <${friend}>.`,
  }), fetch);
```

On CSS 7.2 with ACP:

```text
shared via acp (http://localhost:3001/alice45887/notes/first.acr); bob GET: 200, WAC-Allow null; alice: 200, WAC-Allow null
setAgentAccess returned null
bob GET: 403 null; alice: 200 null
```

No response carried `WAC-Allow`."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-12a> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-12b> .

<#q-read-an-app-12a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "On Community Solid Server 7.2 (2026) configured with ACP, how does the Solid Notes example app's `shareNote` know to write an ACP policy instead of a WAC rule?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Its `rel=\"acl\"` target is typed `acp:AccessControlResource`"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "CSS links an ACR with `rel=\"acl\"` too; a HEAD on it (even a 404) carries `Link` `rel=\"type\"` `acp:AccessControlResource`, which is how the app tells ACP from WAC."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-read-an-app-12a-d1> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-12a-d2> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-12a-d3> .

<#q-read-an-app-12a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Its `WAC-Allow` header lists `acp` as one of the modes"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "CSS 7.2 with ACP sent no WAC-Allow at all, and WAC-Allow has no ACP mode anyway."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-12a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "The access resource's URL ends in `.acr`, not `.acl`"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "URL suffixes are a server convention; clients must not rely on them."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-12a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "The storage description says which access language it uses"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "It declares no access language; the app checks the access resource's own type link."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-12b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "In a Solid app, Inrupt's `universalAccess.setAgentAccess` returns `null` when the app shares a note. What should the app do?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Treat it as not shared: tell the user, or write the rules itself"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "A null result means the access could not be read or set; on a fresh CSS 7.2 ACP resource (2026) the library gave up, while a hand-written N3 Patch to the ACR worked."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-read-an-app-12b-d1> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-12b-d2> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-12b-d3> .

<#q-read-an-app-12b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Carry on: `null` means the access was set and nothing came back"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "On CSS 7.2 with ACP bob stayed at 403; null means the library could not set the access."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-12b-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Retry the same call until it returns an access object"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The ACR is still missing, so the same call fails the same way."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-12b-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Grant the friend Read on the pod root instead, which always works"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That shares everything in the pod, not one note."@en .

<#ch-read-an-app-13>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 12 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## What differs between servers

Code that passes on one server may fail on another (Step 12.13). The table adds node-solid-server (NSS) 6.0.0, recorded by the course authors in 2026. NSS 6 can't log a script in, so those runs used its open root anonymously.

| Behaviour | CSS 7.2 (WAC) | NSS 6.0.0 | CSS 7.2 (ACP) |
|---|---|---|---|
| ETag on GET | yes | **none** | yes |
| Wrong `If-Match` on PATCH | 412 | **200 (ignored)** | 412 |
| Blank node in `solid:inserts` | 422 | **200** | 422 |
| POST `Slug: first` | `first` | **`first.ttl`** | `first` |
| WebSocketChannel2023 | yes | **no** | yes |
| `rel="acl"` points to | ACL | ACL | **ACR** |
| `setAgentAccess` | worked | not tested | **returned null** |

The app uses **feature detection**, never the server's name:

- **No ETag:** send no `If-Match`; stale deletes still fail with 409, and `editNote` retries.
- **No notification service:** `subscribe` returns `null`; the app asks for a reload.
- **An ACR behind `rel="acl"`:** write an ACP policy, not a WAC rule.

On NSS 6.0.0 the same code recorded:

```text
Location: http://localhost:3902/alice40639/notes/first.ttl
edit that lost a race, then retried: {"status":200,"attempt":2,"retriedAfter":409,"conditional":false}
no WebSocketChannel2023 service: the app falls back to reloading by hand
```"""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-13a> .

<#q-read-an-app-13a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "On node-solid-server 6.0.0 (2026), which sends no ETag, the Solid Notes example app's N3 Patch edit lost a race, yet the other user's change survived. What stopped the lost update?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "The stale `solid:deletes` no longer matched, so NSS sent 409"@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "An N3 Patch whose deletes aren't all in the document fails with 409, so deleting the old text acts as a check even without ETags; `editNote` then rereads and retries."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-read-an-app-13a-d1> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-13a-d2> ,
                          <#q-read-an-app-13a-d3> .

<#q-read-an-app-13a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "NSS honoured the `If-Match` header and answered 412"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "NSS 6 sends no ETag on GET, so there was no If-Match, and it ignores a wrong one."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-13a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "NSS locks a document while a client has it open"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "HTTP servers keep no such locks between requests."@en .

<#q-read-an-app-13a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "A WebSocket notification warned the app before it patched"@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "NSS 6 offered no WebSocketChannel2023."@en .

<#ch-read-an-app-14>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 13 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## When a session ends: expiry and one silent restore

The library (authn-browser 5.0.1) renews the access token 5 s before it ends (CSS 7.2 gave 3600 s tokens). If a refresh is refused, the library fires `sessionExpired` and logs out locally (Step 12.7).

Solid Notes then tries one **silent restore**: a new login at the same provider with `prompt: 'none'` ("show no page"). If the provider still has her session (a cookie), the browser comes back with an authorization code (Step 7.6); if not, with `login_required`. Before leaving, the app sets a mark in `sessionStorage`, next to the saved route and draft (Step 12.8). Back with the mark but no session, or failing before leaving, it shows "Log in again". Every page load reads and removes the mark.

⚠ `restorePreviousSession` can't do this: the session is already forgotten. `login()` passes `prompt` on, though its typings omit it.

```js
// src/login.js
export function onExpiry(storage, { restore, prompt }) {
  const ask = () => { storage.removeItem(KEY.restoring); return prompt(); };
  return () => {
    if (storage.getItem(KEY.restoring) !== null) return ask(); // the attempt came back without a session
    storage.setItem(KEY.restoring, new Date().toISOString()); // KEY.restoring is 'solid-notes:restoring'
    return new Promise((resolve) => { resolve(restore()); }).catch(ask); // it failed before leaving
  };
}
```

On CSS 7.2, in a browser test that cut the first token to 20 s and refused the refresh itself: with the provider session alive, the app came back with no password or consent page; with its cookies cleared, one silent attempt, then "Your session has ended. Log in again; your draft is kept." Draft and route survived."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-14a> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-14b> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-14c> .

