<#ch-read-an-app-15>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 14 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Logging out: the app, or the provider too

Step 12.8 gave two levels of logout; Solid Notes has a button for each.

**Log out** (`logoutType: 'app'`) forgets the session in this tab, but the provider still knows the user. On CSS 7.2, a silent login (`prompt=none`) right afterwards still got an authorization code: the provider would have let her straight back in.

**Log out of the provider too** (`'idp'`) also ends the provider's session. The library sends the browser to the provider's `end_session_endpoint`, listed in its `/.well-known/openid-configuration` (Step 7.6), with `id_token_hint`, her ID token (Step 7.5), so the provider knows whose session to end, and `post_logout_redirect_uri`, where to send her afterwards. The provider accepts only a URL the app registered for this (Step 14.16). CSS 7.2 asked to confirm; afterwards a silent login got `login_required`.

⚠ CSS 7.2 still skipped the password at the next login: it keeps a separate `css-account` cookie for its account pages until you log out there.

```js
// src/login.js
export const logOut = () => logout({ logoutType: 'app' });

export function logOutEverywhere(appUrl, storage = sessionStorage) {
  const issuer = storage.getItem(KEY.issuer);
  const registered = issuer && 'clientId' in clientOptions(appUrl, issuer, { dev: dev() });
  storage.removeItem(KEY.issuer);
  return logout({ logoutType: 'idp', ...(registered ? { postLogoutUrl: redirectUrl(appUrl) } : {}) });
}
```

On CSS 7.2:

```text
after app logout, a prompt=none request gets a code
provider logout went to http://localhost:3000/.oidc/session/end with id_token_hint, post_logout_redirect_uri
after provider logout, a prompt=none request gets login_required
but logging in again shows the consent page: CSS still has its own account cookie, css-account
after logging out on CSS's account pages, logging in shows the password page
```"""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-15a> .

