<#ch-read-an-app-16>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 15 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Going live: a Client ID Document and one redirect page

Served the way it would go live (Step 13.9), the app provides two things.

**A Client ID Document** at `/id.jsonld`, built from the origin (scheme, host, port) it is served at, so `client_id` equals its own URL. The app logs in with it when it is on https, or when app and provider are both on `http://localhost`; the development server keeps `clientName` (Step 12.9). The provider fetches the document itself.

**One fixed redirect page**, `/`, listed in `redirect_uris` for logins and in `post_logout_redirect_uris` for provider logout (Step 14.15). The route travels in `sessionStorage` (Step 14.14).

Vite's preview server builds the document on each request; for a static host, the build must write `id.jsonld` for the app's real origin, or the file is missing.

```js
// src/client-id.js
export function clientIdDocument(origin) {
  const start = new URL('/', origin).href; // the one fixed redirect page
  return {
    '@context': ['https://www.w3.org/ns/solid/oidc-context.jsonld'],
    client_id: clientIdUrl(origin),
    client_name: CLIENT_NAME,
    redirect_uris: [start],
    post_logout_redirect_uris: [start],
    scope: 'openid profile offline_access webid',
    // …
  };
}
```

On CSS 7.2 (2026), with the app at `http://localhost:5173`:

```text
GET http://localhost:5173/id.jsonld: 200 application/ld+json; client_id http://localhost:5173/id.jsonld
authorize with client_id http://localhost:5173/id.jsonld: 303 -> http://localhost:3000/.account/
the same, redirect_uri http://localhost:5173/callback (not listed): 400 … "error":"invalid_redirect_uri" …
client_id http://127.0.0.1:5173/id.jsonld: 500 … "SSL is required for client_id authentication unless working locally." …
token_type DPoP, expires_in 3600 s, refresh_token yes
```"""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-16a> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-16b> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-16c> .

<#q-read-an-app-16a>
