<#ch-read-an-app-17>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 16 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Serving it with a CSP

Vite's preview server also sends a **Content-Security-Policy header**: Step 13.2's policy, with the http pods' origins added to `img-src`, and their `http:` and `ws:` origins to `connect-src`. Step 13.2's `https:` and `wss:` don't match a pod on plain http; an https pod needs nothing extra.

Styles live in `src/style.css`, not in an inline `<style>`, because `default-src 'self'` also covers styles and blocks inline ones. The development server sends no CSP: it injects inline styles.

A browser test watched six browser sessions, live updates over WebSocket included, and saw no CSP violations. A real host sends the header from its own configuration.

```js
// vite.config.js
// pods: the pods' plain-http origins, read from VITE_SOLID_BASE when the preview starts
export const csp = [
  "default-src 'self'",
  "script-src 'self'",
  "object-src 'none'",
  "base-uri 'none'",
  `img-src 'self' https: data: ${pods.join(' ')}`,
  `connect-src 'self' https: wss: ${pods.map((o) => `${o} ${o.replace(/^http/, 'ws')}`).join(' ')}`,
].join('; ');
```

With pods at `http://localhost:3000` and `http://localhost:3001` the header read:

```text
default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; img-src 'self' https: data: http://localhost:3000 http://localhost:3001; connect-src 'self' https: wss: http://localhost:3000 ws://localhost:3000 http://localhost:3001 ws://localhost:3001
```"""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-17a> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-17b> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-17c> .

<#q-read-an-app-17a>
