<#ch-read-an-app-18>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-read-an-app> ;
    schema:position 17 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Who logged in: checking the issuer

A login at a provider the profile doesn't list can succeed, but pods won't accept the token as that WebID (Step 7.9). The course authors produced one with two CSS 7.2 servers. CSS lets an account link a WebID from another server once that WebID's profile holds a one-time verification triple (`solid:oidcIssuerRegistrationToken`). So an account on the ACP server linked frank's WebID from the WAC server, and logging in there brought "frank" back from an issuer his profile doesn't list.

So after each login the app compares that issuer with the profile's `solid:oidcIssuer` values, as exact strings. The library doesn't expose the issuer, so `startLogin` saves the provider's own `issuer` string, from its `/.well-known/openid-configuration`, in `sessionStorage`. On a mismatch the app logs out and explains.

```js
// src/login.js
export async function checkIssuer(webId, storage, fetchFn = fetch) {
  const issuer = storage.getItem(KEY.issuer);
  if (!issuer) return { checked: false };
  const listed = await issuersOf(webId, fetchFn);
  return { checked: true, issuer, listed, ok: listed.includes(issuer) }; // exact strings
}
// src/main.js, after every login
  if (issuer.checked && !issuer.ok) {
    await logOut();
```

On CSS 7.2 the app showed:

```text
You logged in at http://localhost:3001/, but the profile of http://localhost:3000/frank54192/profile/card#me lists http://localhost:3000/. Pods won't accept this login as that WebID, so you have been logged out. Log in at a provider your profile lists.
```

That fetch of `/.well-known/openid-configuration` is a connection, so the CSP's `connect-src` must allow every http provider the app may use."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-read-an-app-18a> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-18b> ,
                         <#q-read-an-app-18c> .

