<#q-app-walkthrough-9a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "The SHACL shapes reject every subject that has the old property."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Old data still uses it and must stay readable; the warning is for new code."@en .

<#q-app-walkthrough-9a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "The constant is removed from the generated file once deprecated."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Deprecated terms are kept, because old data in pods still uses them."@en .

<#ch-app-walkthrough-10>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-app-walkthrough> ;
    schema:position 9 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Shapes and migrations in code

Step 11.12 gives the rules; here is where they live:

- **Shapes**: one SHACL file per class and version, open, and without
  `sh:targetClass`, since every version of a class would target the same
  subjects. The validator, in the `shacl` package, picks the shape by
  `rdf:type` plus `sm:formatVersion` (absent means 1).
- **Migrations**: pure modules in the domain package, one per step, typed by
  the generated per-version records, so a step that forgets a required field
  does not compile:

```ts
export const DECK_2_TO_3: MigrationStep<"deck", 2, 3> = {
  shape: "deck", from: 2, to: 3,
  up: ({ direction, ...data }, { subject }) => ({ ...data,
    studyDirection: conceptOfDirection(direction), /* … */ }),
};
```"""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-app-walkthrough-10a> .

<#q-app-walkthrough-10a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "Solid Memo keeps one SHACL shape per class and format version. Why do those shapes leave out `sh:targetClass`?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Each version's shape would target the same subjects, so all but one would fail."@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "With several versions per class, the app picks the shape from the subject's type and `sm:formatVersion` instead of letting every shape target every subject."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-app-walkthrough-10a-d1> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-10a-d2> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-10a-d3> .

