<#ch-app-walkthrough-11>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-app-walkthrough> ;
    schema:position 10 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## The bulk upgrade in code

When an instance's documents need a new format, `solidInstanceCopier.ts`
copies the whole instance to `<name>-<uuid>/`, upgrading as it goes, and only
then switches the type index registrations to the copy:

1. **A write fence.** While the copy runs, the tab's own writes under the
   original are refused before any request leaves the browser.
2. **A check that nothing changed.** The fence cannot stop other tabs or
   apps. So each original document is asked about again with
   `If-None-Match: <the ETag it was copied at>`. A `304` means it is still
   that version; anything else means someone wrote to it, and the run stops
   before the switch. (Without an ETag, `Last-Modified` or a hash of the
   body stands in.)
3. **One commit point.** The switch of the registrations is the moment the
   copy becomes the instance. The original stays as a backup, so a stored
   instance URL can go stale."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-app-walkthrough-11a> .

<#q-app-walkthrough-11a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "While Solid Memo's bulk upgrade (2026) copies Alice's instance to a new container, code in the same browser tab tries to save a review under the original container. What happens?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "The write fence refuses it before the request leaves the browser."@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "A write to the original after it was copied would be lost at the switch; the fence blocks this tab's writes, and the `If-None-Match` check before the switch catches writes from anywhere else."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-app-walkthrough-11a-d1> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-11a-d2> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-11a-d3> .

