    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "The pod refuses it, because the copier has locked the original container."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Solid has no locks; the fence is in the app and covers this tab only."@en .

<#q-app-walkthrough-11a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It is saved, and the copier merges it into the copy afterwards."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "Nothing is merged; a review saved from another tab meanwhile is caught by the check and stops the run."@en .

<#q-app-walkthrough-11a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It is sent to the copy instead, since the copy becomes the instance."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "The fence refuses writes; it does not reroute them."@en .

<#ch-app-walkthrough-12>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-app-walkthrough> ;
    schema:position 11 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Testing across servers

Step 12.13 said to test on several servers. Solid Memo's end-to-end suite runs
its use cases and Solid adapters against servers it starts in Docker, and
separate user journeys drive the built app in a browser against CSS 7:

| Tier | Servers |
|---|---|
| Blocking (gates CI and deploys) | Community Solid Server 6 and 7, node-solid-server 5 and 6 |
| Advisory (reported) | CSS 8 alpha, Pivot (solidcommunity.net's server), Solid-Nextcloud (Nextcloud 32), JavaScript Solid Server (JSS) |

An advisory server keeps an `expected-failures.json`; a job fails only on a
failure it does not list. Tests ask each server instead of assuming: its
`Accept-Patch`, its `Link rel="acl"`.

Some deviations found this way, as of October 2026:

- **Community Solid Server 6** ETags change at most once per second.
- **JSS** drops a language tag on a SPARQL Update insert.
- **Solid-Nextcloud**'s `DELETE DATA` deletes every value of the subject and
  predicate.

Step 16.3 weighs what such deviations mean. Step 15.13 shows how the write code copes
with node-solid-server."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-app-walkthrough-12a> .

<#q-app-walkthrough-12a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "In 2026, Solid Memo tests against several Solid servers, and each advisory server keeps an `expected-failures.json`. What does an entry in it record?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "A known failure of that server, so only new failures break the job."@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Listing known server deviations turns \"red\" into \"something changed\", and the job's summary shows a listed test that now passes, so it can come off the list."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-app-walkthrough-12a-d1> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-12a-d2> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-12a-d3> .

