    solid-memo:distractorNote "Entries record how the server behaves, not defects in the app."@en .

<#ch-app-walkthrough-13>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-app-walkthrough> ;
    schema:position 12 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Writing to node-solid-server

node-solid-server is a blocking server, so every write of Step 15.7 must work
there too. It differs in its ETags, recorded below, and in its PATCH parsing
and size limit, which Solid Memo's code records.

On node-solid-server 6.0.0 (October 2026), an existing Turtle document
answered:

```text
GET    Accept: text/turtle           200, no ETag
HEAD   Accept: text/turtle           200, ETag: W/"2-nOO9…" (of the empty body)
GET    Accept: application/ld+json   200, ETag: W/"a0-XxGgUYFG…"
PATCH  If-Match: "not-the-etag"      200, patch applied
PUT    If-Match: "not-the-etag"      204, document replaced
PUT    If-None-Match: *              412 Precondition Failed
```

- **ETags.** A GET of the document as stored carries no ETag. The weak ones
  on HEAD, on writes and on a converted GET are hashes of that response's
  body, not of the resource. `If-Match` is ignored; `If-None-Match: *` is
  honoured by node-solid-server 5.8.8 and 6.0.0, not by 5.7.4. `saveDataset`
  never puts a weak ETag in `If-Match`, so there it writes without the
  header, and the digest (Step 15.6) has nothing to stamp.
- **PATCH bodies.** It fails to parse the body `@inrupt/solid-client` writes,
  so Solid Memo writes its own, one triple per line.
- **PATCH size.** It reads at most 100 kB of a PATCH, so on every server
  Solid Memo sends an edit over 64 KiB as one PUT of the document *as read*
  plus the change, which keeps other apps' triples. With a strong ETag that
  PUT carries `If-Match`; here it cannot, so a change saved elsewhere since
  the read is lost."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-app-walkthrough-13a> ,
                         <#q-app-walkthrough-13b> .

<#q-app-walkthrough-13a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "On node-solid-server 6.0.0 (2026), a plain Turtle GET returns no ETag and `If-Match` is ignored. What follows for Solid Memo, which caches facts by ETag, on that server?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "Its edits there cannot be conditional, and the digest cache saves nothing."@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Without an ETag there is nothing to put in `If-Match` and nothing to stamp digest facts with, so every visit reads everything; creations stay safe because `If-None-Match: *` is honoured."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-app-walkthrough-13a-d1> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-13a-d2> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-13a-d3> .

