<#q-app-walkthrough-13b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:front "On node-solid-server 6.0.0 (2026), which sends no strong ETag, Solid Memo saves a 70 KiB edit of a large deck as one PUT of the document as read plus the change. What does that PUT keep, and what can it lose?"@en ;
    solid-memo:back "It keeps other apps' triples, but loses a change saved elsewhere since the read."@en ;
    solid-memo:backNote "The PUT is built from the document as read, so other apps' triples stay; without `If-Match` it cannot detect a concurrent change, which a PATCH of the delta would simply have kept."@en ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-app-walkthrough-13b-d1> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-13b-d2> ,
                          <#q-app-walkthrough-13b-d3> .

